The namespace `secure-web` contains the Deployment `secure-app`, exposed by a Service of the same name, and the TLS Secret `web-tls` (certificate for `secure-app.company.com`).

The ingress controller installed in the cluster is Traefik (IngressClass `traefik`), together with its CRDs (for example `Middleware`).

Create an Ingress named `secure-ingress` in `secure-web` that:

- routes the host `secure-app.company.com`, path `/`, to the Service `secure-app`;
- terminates TLS with the existing Secret `web-tls`;
- uses the ingress class `traefik`;
- forces SSL: every plain HTTP request for the host must be redirected to HTTPS.

The security team found that Pods in the namespace `threat-prevention` try to connect to known malicious IP ranges used for command and control servers.

Create a NetworkPolicy named `block-malicious-egress` in `threat-prevention` that:

- applies to all Pods of the namespace;
- blocks **egress** traffic to the ranges `192.168.100.0/24` and `10.0.99.0/24`;
- still allows DNS (UDP 53 and TCP 53) to any destination, even inside those ranges;
- allows all other egress traffic;
- does not affect ingress traffic.

The Dockerfile of an API server is `/tmp/exam/mhagou-008-q5/api-server.Dockerfile` (next to the binary `app-server`, on the jumphost). Modify it to reduce the attack surface of the image:

- use `gcr.io/distroless/base` as the base image;
- copy only the `app-server` binary, to `/app/server`;
- run the container as the distroless non-root user (`nonroot`, UID `65532`);
- configure `/app/server` as the entrypoint, in exec form;
- remove every package installation, shell setup or other unnecessary instruction.

Do not build the image and do not deploy anything.
